# MVP TODO

## Product decisions

- [x] Python bot
- [x] Docker deployment
- [x] Local storage for normal operation
- [x] The user's private bot chat as an off-container backup store
- [x] Single-GIF saving only
- [x] No Telegram user credentials
- [ ] Decide whether the bot is private to one owner or shared with an allowlist
- [ ] Decide default backup interval and retention count

## Bot behavior

- [ ] Add `/start` and `/help` with the full command list
- [ ] Register Telegram command suggestions in BotFather-compatible form
- [ ] Add an inline-keyboard main menu
- [ ] Accept GIFs sent directly and forwarded from another chat
- [ ] Implement a save conversation with cancel support
- [ ] Compute a SHA-256 hash before storing a GIF
- [ ] Return the existing GIF when an exact duplicate is detected
- [ ] Add optional tags and categories during saving
- [ ] Implement paginated browsing with inline buttons
- [ ] Implement tag search and random GIF retrieval
- [ ] Handle unsupported media and large files clearly

## Persistence

- [ ] Define SQLite schema for GIFs, hashes, tags, and backup records
- [ ] Store media and database below `/data`
- [ ] Create atomic local writes and startup integrity checks
- [ ] Build a versioned compressed backup archive
- [ ] Make `/backup` send the current user's archive to the current bot chat
- [ ] Validate backup checksum and archive contents before restore
- [ ] Accept `/restore` only as a reply to a bot-created backup document
- [ ] Validate checksum, ownership, and archive contents before restore
- [ ] Keep existing data untouched if restore validation fails
- [ ] Add confirmed manual `/backup` and reply-based `/restore` actions
- [ ] Add periodic backups and configurable retention

## Docker and operations

- [ ] Add `Dockerfile`
- [ ] Add `docker-compose.yml` with a `/data` volume
- [ ] Add `.env.example` with `BOT_TOKEN` and storage settings
- [ ] Add health logging and graceful shutdown
- [ ] Document private bot-chat backup and restore setup
- [ ] Document backup security and recovery procedure

## Testing

- [ ] Test hash-based duplicate detection
- [ ] Test backup creation and checksum validation
- [ ] Test restore into an empty data directory
- [ ] Test failed restore leaves existing data untouched
- [ ] Test command handlers and inline keyboard callbacks
- [ ] Test the Docker image with a mounted volume

## Later, explicitly out of scope

- [ ] Bulk import of historical chat GIFs
- [ ] Telethon or another Telegram user-account client
- [ ] Approximate duplicate detection
- [ ] Cloud storage
